Package: mica-ssh
Version: 2025.89-mica3
Source-Date-Epoch: 1792823171
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: dropbear-bin, mica-system
Provides: mica-ssh-server
Conflicts: mica-openssh
Description: Mica OS SSH: dropbear, started at boot as micad last configured it
 SSH as an option on the floor, in place of mica-openssh's OpenSSH:
 mica-sshd.service, its prestart /usr/lib/mica/mica-sshd-prestart and the
 preset that enables the unit. It starts at boot when the settings micad saves
 in /var/lib/mica/ssh/sshd.env on DATA turn SSH on, with or without micad, and
 is off until they do; micad restarts it for new settings and stops it. The
 prestart translates the settings into dropbear's arguments, and mica-dropbear-prestart makes the ed25519 host key on
 the STATE partition at the first start. The unit requires
 mica-shadow-reconcile.service, so the shadow file is built in RAM before a
 login can read it. dropbear.service, started the same way after
 /run/mica/dropbear.env, is the same server under the name micad used before.
 .
 dropbear authenticates through crypt(3) against /etc/shadow, not through PAM:
 the build refuses a pinned dropbear-bin that depends on PAM or whose binary
 names libpam.
 .
 On an OpenRC root the same services are /etc/init.d/mica-sshd and
 /etc/init.d/mica-dropbear, in no runlevel; mica-sshd-boot, in the default
 runlevel, starts mica-sshd at boot when the saved settings turn SSH on.
